# Template for /etc/vmguard/secrets.env  (chmod 600, owned by vmguard user)
# Fill in the real value, then save as secrets.env in the staging dir.
# NEVER commit with a real value; NEVER place this secret inside the guest.
#
# Two credentials are held host-side, both injected by the addon and neither ever
# placed in the guest. Under design "B" the Anthropic credential is a Pro/Max
# subscription token that lives IN THE GUEST (see guest-setup.sh), so there is no
# Anthropic secret here.
GH_PAT=github_pat_REPLACE_ME

# CircleCI personal API token — OPTIONAL. Used for exactly one thing: injecting auth on
# POST /api/v2/workflow/{id}/rerun so the guest can retry failed CI jobs (NOTES 43).
# CircleCI reads need no token (vxsuite is public) and get none.
#
# DELETE THIS LINE if you don't want that: the gate starts and runs fine without it, and
# reruns are simply denied ("no CIRCLE_TOKEN configured host-side") until it's set.
#
# It must be a PERSONAL token — CircleCI does not accept project-scoped tokens on API v2 —
# so it is account-wide by nature. The addon, not the token, is what narrows it to one
# endpoint in one set of orgs. Mint at: circleci.com → User Settings → Personal API Tokens.
CIRCLE_TOKEN=CCIPAT_REPLACE_ME
